/* A safe-area is a column of its own natural height, like on web (base-css)
   and Flutter: it does not grow by itself. As the app's root it fills the
   page through the compiler's .fjs-page-root class; inside a navbar it is
   just the bar plus the status-bar strip.
   min-height: 0 everywhere: the webview renderer follows CSS, where a column
   flex item is at least as tall as its content — as a page root that broke
   the height chain, the shell's scroll-view grew to the whole content and
   the window scrolled instead (navbar and all). Skyline has no such minimum.
   The root fills the host (auto basis: a natural-height host still sizes to
   the content) and carries the insets as inline padding. */
:host {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  min-height: 0;
}
.fjs-safe-area-root {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  flex-grow: 1;
  flex-shrink: 1;
  flex-basis: auto;
  min-width: 0;
  min-height: 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
